  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = 500(1.2)^{x}\\). The function \\(g\\) is defined by \\(g(x) = f(x + 1)\\). For all values of \\(x\\), \\(g(x) = k \\cdot f(x)\\), where \\(k\\) is a constant. What is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "1.2"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "\\(g(x) = f(x + 1) = 500(1.2)^{x + 1} = 500(1.2)^{x} \\cdot 1.2\\).",
    "So \\(g(x) = 1.2 \\cdot f(x)\\), and \\(k = 1.2\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nf = 500*Rational('1.2')**x\nk = simplify(f.subs(x, x + 1)/f)\nassert k == Rational(6, 5)\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0]) == k",
